    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Scent molecules have no gender. Rose smells extraordinary on masculine skin when anchored by smoky oud, and dry cedarwood radiates with chic elegance on feminine skin. Master perfumers in Paris and Grasse have always created for the nose, not the gender box.</p><p>Here is why unisex fragrance has taken over Britain and how to find a signature scent that transcends tired marketing tropes.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "editorial--text-section",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Gendered Department Store Marketing vs Pure Olfactory Craft",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Traditional fragrance marketing relied on superficial archetypes: hyper-sexualised commercials, celebrity ambassadors, and rigid packaging codes designed to tell shoppers what they 'should' like.</p><p>It forced people into narrow olfactory boxes and discouraged men from exploring warm florals or women from experiencing rich woods.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>Unisex luxury perfumery removes the packaging theatrics and focuses entirely on the complexity of the juice: saffron, ambergris, bergamot, smoky vetiver, and clean musk.</p><p>These notes adapt dynamically to your personal skin chemistry, smelling distinct, intriguing, and bespoke on everyone who wears them.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
